From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: restore facts().draft_confidence, dropped by the port

The pin sets `draft_confidence = if (block) null else self.mtp_confidence` (a drafter
ignores it; otherwise it is the --mtp-confidence value). The ported facts() literal had
lost the line entirely, so every GLM lane ran with a null confidence: a default-path
regression that `copy_drafts_cuda_test` caught as `expected 0.7, found null`.

A field-by-field diff of the pin facts() Model literal against the ported one now shows
no pin field missing; the only extra fields are the three knobs 0026 wired
(free_shared, plain_margin) plus many_resumed.

Gates on pin+0001..0030: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new, test-cuda-host drops that failure (2 to 1) with no new ones.
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
index 11ac31746..1b97f7597 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ pub const Lanes = struct {
             .draft_streams = block, // one block pass drafts every stream of the round
             .mtp_step_ms = if (block) 1.6 / @as(f64, max_held) else 0,
             .draft_probabilities = block, // the selector's chances size each window against the costs below
+            .draft_confidence = if (block) null else self.mtp_confidence, // a drafter ignores it; otherwise --mtp-confidence
             .window_costs = if (block) (if (self.timed) |*t| &t.window else &gb10_window_costs) else &.{},
             .shared_costs = if (block) (if (self.timed) |*t| &t.shared else &gb10_shared_costs) else &.{},
             // TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE: a shared round's windows take no cost model, so they fill likeliest-first
